{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1776790413,"nonce":"1ZiOrRkmUosPbSNhoqmr+NpJ8fc=","title":"Stale review sessions not cleaned up after watcher restart","message":"## Problem\n\nReview sessions can get stuck in an inconsistent state after watcher restart:\n- `completed_at` is set (review finished)\n- Session directory still exists\n- Watcher loops trying to launch new review, fails with \"session already exists\"\n\n## Root Cause\n\nRace condition between container exit and watcher cleanup:\n\n1. Review container sets `completed_at` and exits\n2. Watcher should poll, detect verdict, call `cleanup_review_session()`\n3. If watcher restarts/crashes between steps 1 and 2, cleanup is lost\n\n## Example (2026-04-21)\n\nSession `review-b7e7dee7b0bd` had:\n```json\n{\"status\": \"waiting:review\", \"completed_at\": \"2026-04-21T16:15:19.552265+00:00\"}\n```\n\nWatcher log showed repeated failures:\n```\n[b7e7dee7b0bd] Review launch failed -- reverting to waiting:review\nError: session already exists for issue b7e7dee7b0bd...\n```\n\n## Fix\n\nTwo options:\n\n### Option 1: Startup cleanup (preferred)\nOn watcher startup, scan for review sessions with `completed_at` set → clean them up.\n\n### Option 2: Pre-launch check\nIn `maybe_launch_review()`, before launching, check if `review-\u003csid\u003e` exists with `completed_at` set → delete it first.\n\n## Tests\n\n- tests/watcher/test_session_monitor.py::test_startup_cleans_stale_review_sessions\n- tests/watcher/test_review_orchestrator.py::test_launch_review_cleans_stale_session_first\n\n## Files\n\n- host/watcher/session_monitor.py (add startup cleanup)\n- host/watcher/review_orchestrator.py (add pre-launch check in maybe_launch_review)\n\n## Related\n\n- docs/known-issues-watcher-sighup.md (documents this case)\n\nREQ: REQ-019 (review lifecycle)","files":null}]}